# DUNCAN PRIME R02 — TOTAL DEVELOPMENT / SHERIFF / LESTER PROGRAMMING SCHOOL

STATUS = OWNER-DIRECTED / ACTIVE DESIGN+BASE IMPLEMENTATION
PARENT = #206
BASE_MAIN_AT_START = b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1
PRIME_CORE_MUTATION = NO
PRODUCTION_MUTATION = NO
CANON_MUTATION = NO
AUTO_MERGE = NO

## OWNER GOAL

DUNCAN PRIME must develop as one persistent root personality and general creative/technical intelligence shaped by verified experience and OWNER taste evidence, while remaining evidence-bound and fail-closed.

Required capabilities include, by relevance rather than random accumulation:
- SELF_MODEL + OWNER_TASTE_MODEL + episodic/project/world memory;
- meta-learning and learning how to learn;
- teaching/evaluating other agents;
- SHERIFF control, discipline, incident learning and internal scoreboards;
- administration, project command, research, strategy, security and operations;
- mathematics, geometry, statistics, optimization, physics, computer science and engineering;
- visual art, directing, animation, VFX, sound, editing, writing and worldbuilding;
- critical thinking, philosophy, psychology, economics, licensing and communication;
- continuous open-source study with changed/unseen transfer before skill promotion.

## LESTER RELATIONSHIP

`LESTER = DUNCAN PRIME PERSONAL PROGRAMMING ASSISTANT`

DUNCAN is responsible for LESTER's programming curriculum, review, error analysis and skill development. LESTER performs bounded real programming work; DUNCAN teaches from evidence and SHERIFF tracks discipline independently.

Learning path:
`REAL ZORR TASK -> EVIDENCE -> TEST/QC -> ERROR/SUCCESS CLASSIFICATION -> LESSON -> CHANGED/UNSEEN TRANSFER -> SKILL UPDATE`

LESTER must learn primarily from:
`EXISTING ZORR CODE -> NATIVE/STANDARD PLATFORM -> MATURE OSS SOURCE+TESTS -> MINIMAL ZORR GLUE`.

## REUSE BASE — DO NOT REBUILD

Mandatory existing foundations:
1. Permanent Archive V1 / `zb-archive-v1` RAW evidence.
2. DUNCAN Fortress R01 / `DUNCAN_CONTEXT_NEXT_V1` fail-closed derived learning.
3. SHERIFF V1 / verdict history + discipline/skill scoreboard + production runtime.
4. PR #205 Unified Archive Restore V1 sandbox patterns: SQLite FTS5 retrieval, CLOSED-verdict verified lessons, deterministic training corpus, optimized policy guarded by conflict detection.
5. Existing GitHub Actions / tests / direct GitHub connector.

Do not add a second archive, second scheduler, second DB service, generic custom agent framework, or proprietary memory layer.

## OSS STUDY BASIS

Use mature upstream code only when it fills a proven gap. Current high-value references for programming training/evaluation include SWE-bench, SWE-agent/mini-SWE-agent, OpenHands core/eval patterns, pytest, Hypothesis, Ruff, Pyright, Bandit/maintained security linters, plus existing actionlint/zizmor/Gitleaks.

Adoption is not automatic; inspect exact source/tests/license and prefer extracting patterns over importing heavy frameworks.

## R02 BASE-FIRST SCOPE

First implementable base is intentionally narrow:

`DUNCAN -> LESTER PROGRAMMING SCHOOL + DOMAIN SKILL MODEL`

It must:
- keep SHERIFF discipline separate from competence;
- add domain/task-kind skill state for LESTER instead of one meaningless global score;
- derive training candidates only from durable evidence and verified outcomes;
- never self-promote from reading or one successful task;
- require changed/unseen transfer for PROVEN/OPERATIONAL-style promotion;
- preserve neutral bootstrap where historical evidence is insufficient;
- expose a deterministic next-training-target view for DUNCAN;
- remain rebuildable and auditable;
- use existing code/tests and standard library first.

## BASE PASS

`LESTER_PROGRAMMING_SCHOOL_R01 = PASS` only when a fresh candidate proves:
- exact current-main base binding;
- deterministic schema/profile for per-domain programming skills;
- no fabricated historical scores;
- SHERIFF discipline remains independent;
- changed/unseen transfer gate enforced;
- deterministic next-target selection;
- regression tests cover no-self-promotion and insufficient-evidence fail-closed behavior;
- repository validation/full tests pass on exact HEAD;
- fresh GitHub readback matches exact candidate;
- main remains unchanged until separate merge authorization.

After this base passes, future R02 slices may expand OWNER understanding, meta-learning, agent school, math/science curricula and other domains one proven slice at a time.
